{#
  T-7.06 / T-7.07 — the tag row under a story.

  Usage:
    {% include 'components.stories.story-tags' with { story: item } only %}

  EXTRACTED IN T-7.07, NOT INVENTED BY IT. The row was written inline in
  `story-card.twig`; the story view draws the same chips under the same image, so
  it moved here rather than being typed a second time. Doc 15 forbids the second
  copy, and the tag row is exactly the size of thing that gets copied because
  copying it looks cheaper than a file.

  THE BRAND COMES FIRST, which in Arabic puts it at the right-hand end of the row
  — the artboard's order on every card in the feed and in the story view.

  NOT CONTROLS. On the feed page these become the filter chips T-7.01 owns; here
  and on Home they are labels. `--border-subtle` is correct for a label and
  becomes a WCAG 1.4.11 failure the moment they can be pressed — the note is in
  `04-components/stories.scss`, at the rule itself.
#}
{% set story_tags = story.tags is defined and story.tags is not empty ? story.tags|split(',') : [] %}

{% if story.brand or story_tags|length %}
    <ul class="story-card__tags" aria-label="{{ trans('theme.stories.tags_label') }}">
        {# `<bdi>` and not a bare span: brand names are Latin runs inside an RTL
           list, and T-1.04's rule is that isolation goes on the inline element
           around the run, never on the block that contains it. #}
        {% if story.brand %}
            <li class="story-card__tag"><bdi>{{ story.brand }}</bdi></li>
        {% endif %}

        {% for tag in story_tags %}
            {% if tag|trim %}
                <li class="story-card__tag">{{ tag|trim }}</li>
            {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
{% endif %}
